# [AUTHOR]: Carlos González Sanz
#
# > The purpose of this file is to store default
# > Compose rules for typing board game symbols
# > that can be input with alphabetical Cyrillic characters
# > by using the "Miscellaneous Symbols" dead key (<U232C>)
# > in conjunction with the Compose Key (<Multi_key>).
#

# Anglo-French Playing Card Symbols
#
# [NOTE]: All symbols listed here are enclosed inside square brackets.
#
# [NOTE]: Each piece does also encode info about its suit and value
#         in the following regex-like notation:
#           
#         regexp = \[([0-9]{,2}|[ЦцЈјԚԛКк])?[(->)|(<3)|(<>)|(\.3)](\*)?\]
#
#         Where:
#         - [ЦцЈјԚԛКк]              = Any non-numerical playing card (Knight/Cavalier -> Jack -> Queen -> King).
#         - (->)|(<3)|(<>)|(\.3)]   = The card's own suit (Spade, Heart, Diamond or Club). Omitting the card's value will output the corresponding suit symbol.
#         - \*                      = Whether the current suit is black. If not entered, it means the current suit is white/red.
#
# [Main source]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Playing_cards_in_Unicode
#
