# Chess Piece Symbols (Excluding Pawns)
#
# [NOTE]: All symbols listed here are enclosed inside square brackets.
#         Additionally, each symbol is represented by their
#         corresponding letter in both the English and Spanish
#         algebraic chess notations whenever possible.
#
# [NOTE]: Each piece does also encode info about its rotation and color
#         in the following regex-like notation:
#           
#         regexp = \[[ABCDEFHKNQRT]*([0-9]{,3})?[*-]?\]
#
#         Where:
#         - [ABCDEFHKNQRT]  = Any orthodox chess piece (including both the alfil and ferz) and some fairy chess pieces. Omitting this field will always produce a pawn.
#         - [0-9]{,3}       = The piece's own rotation measured in sexagesimal degrees (more specifically, in multiples of 45º). The default rotation is 0º.
#         - [*-]            = The piece's own color ("*" for black, "-" for neutral). Leaving this field blank will result in a white piece.
#
# [Main source]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chess_symbols_in_Unicode
#
